A. THE BINDING COUNTS ON THE CUBIC LATTICE, AGAINST NATURE'S RATIOS B / B(deuteron)
   set | bodies | contact Links | each body's contacts | per body (binding-v1 as built) | per contact Link | bilinear in the partners' contacts | nature's B / B(d)
   deuteron | 2 | 1 | [1, 1] | 1.00 | 1.00 | 1.00 | 1.00
   triton (a line) | 3 | 2 | [1, 2, 1] | 1.50 | 2.00 | 4.00 | 3.81
   triton (an L) | 3 | 2 | [1, 2, 1] | 1.50 | 2.00 | 4.00 | 3.47
   alpha (a square) | 4 | 4 | [2, 2, 2, 2] | 2.00 | 4.00 | 16.00 | 12.72
   alpha (a square, with the two diagonals as second neighbours) | 4 | 6 | [3, 3, 3, 3] | 2.00 | 6.00 | 54.00 | 12.72
   (the triton's line and L give the same counts; nature's triton 3.81 and helium-3 3.47 differ by the Coulomb repulsion, not modelled here)

   the saturated crystal (every body with six contacts, three contact Links per body), the binding per nucleon over the deuteron's per pair:
   per contact Link: B / A = 3 gives per body = 6.7 MeV per nucleon against nature's 8.0 (the ratio 0.83); bilinear: 3 x 36 = 108 gives per body = 240 MeV per nucleon (the ratio 30)
   the count per contact Link is right at saturation within 20 percent and short on the alpha by 3; the bilinear count is right on the light nuclei within 25 percent and over at saturation by 30: no single count of the lattice's geometry carries nature's binding from the deuteron to iron

B. THE MASS DEFECT AS A FRACTION OF THE MASS
   the deuteron: nature 0.1186 percent (4.353 m_e of 3674.84); the law's give 4 units of 3677: 0.1088 percent (series N: 0.109, an input width 8 percent under nature)
   the alpha: nature 0.759 percent; the law's give 8 of 7354: 0.109 percent (the ratio to the deuteron 2.0 against 12.72, NATURE row 7b)
   iron: nature about 0.86 percent per nucleon

C. THE LINEARITY THAT FORBIDS A LADDER: a two-body exchange of paid quanta as a linear map on the contents
   (32768, 8192) -> (20480, 20480) after 6000 intervals at the rate 1 / 1024 each way: the total 40960 kept, the difference shrinks by (1 - 2 / 1024) per interval, the equal split the only fixed point of every total
   (20480, 20480) -> (20480, 20480) after 6000 intervals at the rate 1 / 1024 each way: the total 40960 kept, the difference shrinks by (1 - 2 / 1024) per interval, the equal split the only fixed point of every total
   (40000, 960) -> (20480, 20480) after 6000 intervals at the rate 1 / 1024 each way: the total 40960 kept, the difference shrinks by (1 - 2 / 1024) per interval, the equal split the only fixed point of every total
   every rule that acts per unit of content is linear in it (24.2's additivity), so no content is selected: the masses design's theorem; a ladder needs a rule that is not per unit of content (the window against the reader's own clock, which gives a harmonic ladder with 3068 unseen leptons)
